  "reference_anchor_correction": "Canonical Delete line 175 is unrelated explanatory prose. Exact action anchor is OpenExternallyPanel.py138; Add 136 and Edit 137 are correct, supported by table 132/simple-delete and ClientGUIListCtrl1375 prompt.",
  "observations": [
    "Only the outer file_action Delete question changes to Remove all selected?; the captured selected MIME vector, empty/GeneralFile guards and accepted-only staged deletion are unchanged. Nested queue_action remains count-based, matching its separate recording.",
    "Choosers 4/6 full 73-label order, title and sort_tuples=false are compared. GeneralFile is already used; the later used-PNG exclusion is explicitly Qt-source-derived, not falsely attributed to choosers 4/6.",
    "Add/Cancel/Apply and existing PNG Edit/Cancel/Apply replay complete events8\u201311 and nested titles/name vectors. Add selects the sorted PNG identity; standalone and mixed GeneralFile protection replay event 12 and source guard.",
    "Outer question compares exact recorded notice 2, title and notice flags before capture. No preserves full visible draft/selection and Store; Yes removes PNG in event 13, remains staged and is discarded by parent Cancel.",
    "The strengthened saved phase accepts actual Add One/Two\u2192Down and parent Apply, checking full event 9 Routing CallRefs and unchanged Manager. Reopened actual PNG Edit adds OS then Down; child Apply leaves Store at event 9 until parent Apply checks full event 11. Reopen and actual outer Delete then save exact event 13. There is no reseed or reconstruction of the final Edit through Add.",
    "Expected keys decode all 64 hexadecimal characters into 32 bytes. Intermediate table and child assertions expose names and selected flags; they are not observations of opaque native keys. Direct typed Store/reopen assertions establish final keys separately.",
    "Old genuinely pending outer Add chooser and PNG Delete question are retained through parent Cancel against current JPEG Add and GIF Delete successors. All old chosen/Yes/No/Cancel/force-close/root/close actions preserve current full visible draft, complete saved Routing/Manager and current slot identity/visibility. Hidden child/parent attempts are no-ops, show restores admission, current Apply is blocked while child open, and current positive actions still work.",
    "Existing callbacks use weak State/window captures and once-only alive guards. Old cancellation makes later close callbacks no-ops before shared-slot removal; temporary RefCell guards do not survive callbacks. The production change adds no ownership, callback or borrowing behavior.",
    "Each capture retains the adapter belonging to its actual live constructor. Existing bounded routing_capture advances real timers/animations and requires consecutive identical buffers; no property forcing or input retries were introduced."
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "This is source-only review. Exact committed full Linux Clippy/tests/parity and actual six fresh rendered captures remain required; no runtime or rendered approval is granted.",
    "Callbacks drive outer Add/Edit/Delete, nested actions and answers. No physical nested coordinates, full keyboard/column behavior, default/universal geometry or OS focus is established.",
    "The MIME chooser has 73 model entries and a finite scrollable viewport; the screenshot cannot claim all entries are visible. The 520\u00d7440,580\u00d7340,520\u00d7200 and960\u00d7800 captures need fresh readability/Unicode/footer inspection.",
    "Historical Qt PNG is later washed outer mapping context, not a matching new chooser/queue/question state. No nested pixel, placement, decoration or timing parity is claimed.",
    "Ownership evidence is bounded to parent Cancel/replacement, genuine pending outer children, stale callbacks and temporary hide/show recovery. Automatic Main/final Bound destruction, broad page-switch ownership and generic owner guarantees are excluded.",
    "Only the three outer MIME leaves are candidates. No parent, alias, native hierarchy, default route, launch platform, deeper call/process output, legacy import, whole-MIME exhaustion or additional consumer credit."
  ],
